            <div xml:id="d452">

                <pb facs="0564" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2322C</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-11-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 24, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have not heard from
                    you since our conversation in regard to the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lusitania</hi> case. I hope that you have been able to accomplish
                    something. It is imperative that we should reach a speedy settlement of this
                    controversy for the reasons which I stated to you when we talked the matter
                    over. I hope that a conclusion may be reached within a very few days.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
